nodecode-culture is a rewrite of pswong661-eng's pswong661-eng/hermes-global-business-culture:

  https://github.com/pswong661-eng/hermes-global-business-culture
  commit 49218a35f670ceae6f79dc07d40536b19da23cc6
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Eric Wong (pswong661-eng) (LICENSE)

The original is a Hermes Agent plugin: three Python tools (culture_brief,
culture_gap_analysis, culture_countries) computed from two bundled JSON data
files, a /culture command and a practitioner skill. The rewrite keeps the data
(the 57 economies, their Meyer and Hofstede positions, GLOBE cluster and Lewis
type, the highlights, and the 11 regional playbooks) and the arithmetic
unchanged, and reimplements the tools as one Lisp system over the same tables:
the same three tool names, the same /culture command, the same task weights,
misread risks, adaptation moves, aliases and name resolution (exact, alias,
containment, close spelling). The answers are text rather than JSON, since a
model reads the line and a person can too; every field the original's JSON
carried is one of those lines.

Left out: the bundled skill became the cell's manual topic (help :culture),
which every request already knows how to carry, so its doctrine is present
without a second file to load; the Python packaging (plugin.yaml, schemas.py,
pytest suite) and the original's CI drift check have no counterpart, because
the loader, the contracts and the test slice are the host's own.
